Business Rules:-
The system is centered around branches, which manage employees, warehouses, suppliers, supply orders, customers, and customer orders. Each branch must employ multiple employees, where every employee must work in only one branch and has a role such as manager, cashier, or stock keeper, which is assigned to a warehouse, with unique id, name, job title, at least one phone number or more, salary, and hire date. Some employees may supervise others within the same branch. Each branch must operate one or more warehouses, and every warehouse must belong to only one branch, meaning a branch cannot function without at least one warehouse. Each warehouse has unique id, name, phone number. Warehouses are used to store products, where a single product can be stored in different warehouses, and each warehouse may contain multiple products. Products include details such as unique id, name, category, brand, price, stock quantity, and expiry date. Every product must be stored in a warehouse, and no expired product is allowed to be sold. Products must be provided by suppliers, where one supplier can provide many products, and each product comes from a supplier. Suppliers must deal with multiple branches, and each branch can receive products from multiple suppliers. Each supplier has unique id, company, name, at least on phone number. When a branch needs products, it creates a supply order sent to one supplier, including unique id, date, payment method, and total price, while a supplier can receive many such orders from different branches. Customers are served by branches by making orders. Each customer has a unique id, name and phone number and is either Regular or Importer. A customer can place multiple orders, but an order can also exist without a registered customer (walk-in). Each order includes unique id, date, payment method, and total price, and payment method. Orders must include products where an order can contain multiple products, and each product can appear in many orders. Also, branches can serve many customers, and each customer can buy from different branches, and similarly, products can be sold in multiple branches. Business rules ensure that every branch has at least one warehouse, every warehouse belongs to one branch.
